  </section>

  <h2>Read the updated supply note</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Riverside workshop at 8:20</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Seventy-two guests are registered, and eighty chairs are ready. We have twenty-four liters of water in forty-eight bottles. There is a lot of coffee, but only a little setup time remains. We have a few spare badges, enough for the four expected late guests. Few printed maps remain, so the digital map is on the entrance screen. The guide contains a lot of information, and many participants opened it yesterday.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You used the note to distinguish people, substance, units, enough small quantities, and a printed-map shortage.">
    <h3>Reading check: use only the supply note</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="seventy-two guests" data-hint="The opening clause gives the exact registration count." data-fix="Seventy-two guests are registered."><p class="quiz-question">1. How many guests are registered?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="seventy-two guests">seventy-two guests</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="eighty guests">eighty guests</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="forty-eight guests">forty-eight guests</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="twenty-four liters in forty-eight bottles" data-hint="The note reports both the total amount and its countable containers." data-fix="The center has twenty-four liters of water in forty-eight bottles."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which answer gives both the water amount and bottle number?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="twenty-four liters in forty-eight bottles">twenty-four liters in forty-eight bottles</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="forty-eight liters in twenty-four bottles">forty-eight liters in twenty-four bottles</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="seventy-two liters with no bottles">seventy-two liters with no bottles</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="four spare badges are enough" data-hint="A few signals a small positive count, and the note says it covers four late guests." data-fix="Four spare badges are enough for the expected late guests."><p class="quiz-question">3. What does the note imply about spare badges?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="four spare badges are enough">four spare badges are enough</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="there are no spare badges">there are no spare badges</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the badge quantity is excessive">the badge quantity is excessive</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the printed-map count is too small" data-hint="Bare few presents the printed maps as a shortage and motivates the digital display." data-fix="The digital map is displayed because the printed-map count is too small."><p class="quiz-question">4. Why is the digital map on the entrance screen?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the printed-map count is too small">the printed-map count is too small</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the guide contains no information">the guide contains no information</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="too many chairs block the printed maps">too many chairs block the printed maps</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build an amount question and a negative update</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="how many bottles of water do we need" data-hint="Begin with How many because bottles is the countable unit, then complete the question." data-fix="How many bottles of water do we need?" data-success-message="Correct. How many follows the countable unit bottles, while of water names the contents.">
    <h3>Drill 4: count the containers</h3><p class="tile-target">Ask for the number of water containers.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="need">need</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="bottles">bottles</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="water">water</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="how">How</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="of">of</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="many">many</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="we">we</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="do">do</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="there isn't much setup time left" data-hint="Begin with There isn’t, then use much before noncount setup time." data-fix="There isn’t much setup time left." data-success-message="Correct. The negative update uses much before the noncount phrase setup time.">
    <h3>Drill 5: report a small remaining amount</h3><p class="tile-target">The doors open soon. Say that the remaining setup time is small.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="left">left</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="much">much</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="there">There</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="setup">setup</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="isn't">isn’t</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="time">time</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair three different errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="much" data-hint="The question asks for a number of separate guests." data-fix="How many guests are registered?" data-why="Guests is a plural count noun, so use how many." data-success-message="Correct. Separate guests require the count question how many.">
    <h3>Drill 6: count the guests</h3><p>The registration question says: <span class="ex">How much guests are registered?</span> Tap the quantifier with the wrong noun type.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="how">How</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="much">much</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="guests">guests</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="registered">registered</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="lot" data-hint="A noun follows, so the large-quantity expression needs of." data-fix="We have a lot of information in the guide." data-why="Use a lot of before a noun; use a lot only when no noun follows." data-success-message="Correct. The following noun information requires the complete phrase a lot of.">
    <h3>Drill 7: keep <em>of</em> before the noun</h3><p>The guide update says: <span class="ex">We have a lot information in the guide.</span> Tap the incomplete quantity phrase.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we">We</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="have">have</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="lot">a lot</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="information">information</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="guide">in the guide</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="is" data-hint="The noun chairs is plural even though a lot of comes first." data-fix="A lot of chairs are ready." data-why="The noun controls agreement: plural chairs takes are." data-success-message="Correct. Plural chairs, not the quantifier, controls the verb are.">
    <h3>Drill 8: let the noun control the verb</h3><p>The inventory says: <span class="ex">A lot of chairs is ready.</span> Tap the verb with incorrect agreement.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="a">A</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="lot">lot</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="of">of</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="chairs">chairs</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="ready">ready</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Oral transforms: change the package or quantity</h3>
    <p>Say the complete new sentence before revealing it. Preserve the stated fact.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> Ask for the water amount, not its containers.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>How much water do we need?</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Now ask for the number of bottles.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>How many bottles of water do we need?</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> <span class="ex">We have a lot of chairs.</span> Make a compact negative that means the number is small.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>We don’t have many chairs.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> <span class="ex">There is a lot of time.</span> Make a compact negative that means the amount is small.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There isn’t much time.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> The safe limit is ten tables; twelve are in the aisle. Report the excess.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There are too many tables in the aisle.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> The café has two separate coffee servings ready. Use plural <span class="ex">coffees</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Two coffees are ready.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Communicate: solve a fictional supply problem</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real food, drinks, home, work, school, schedule, location, money, purchases, health, body, family, relationships, travel, belongings, or habits. Use the Riverside inventory, invent a neutral public event, or share personal information only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask before planning:</b> Ask two <span class="ex">How many</span> questions about countable supplies and two <span class="ex">How much</span> questions about noncount supplies. Answer with a complete quantity and then a natural short answer.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: give a 45–60 second fictional supply briefing.</b> Include one amount and its countable unit, one large quantity, one useful small number, one useful small amount, one shortage, one zero quantity, and one quantity that passes a stated limit. Make each verb agree with its noun.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Repackage the quantity:</b> Choose water, coffee, information, advice, furniture, or equipment. Describe it once as a noncount amount and once through a countable unit or serving. Explain why the real-world material can stay the same while the grammar changes.</div>

  <h2>Final check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You controlled noncount information, conversational large quantity, shortage meaning, and noun-based agreement.">
    <h3>Four decisions with one defensible target</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="How much information does the guide contain?" data-hint="Information is noncount in this general amount question." data-fix="How much information does the guide contain?"><p class="quiz-question">1. Which question asks for the general amount of information, not a number of separate items?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="How much information does the guide contain?">How much information does the guide contain?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="How many information does the guide contain?">How many information does the guide contain?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="How many informations does the guide contain?">How many informations does the guide contain?</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="We have a lot of equipment." data-hint="The target is neutral everyday positive speech before noncount equipment." data-fix="We have a lot of equipment."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence is the natural everyday positive update about a large equipment quantity?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We have a lot of equipment.">We have a lot of equipment.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We have many equipment.">We have many equipment.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We have a lot equipment.">We have a lot equipment.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the printed-map count is smaller than needed" data-hint="Bare few emphasizes a shortage rather than a useful small count." data-fix="Few printed maps remain means the printed-map count is smaller than needed."><p class="quiz-question">3. The coordinator says, <span class="ex">Few printed maps remain, so display the digital map</span>. What does <span class="ex">few</span> imply?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the printed-map count is smaller than needed">the printed-map count is smaller than needed</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the small map count is definitely enough">the small map count is definitely enough</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="there are too many printed maps">there are too many printed maps</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A lot of chairs are ready." data-hint="Plural chairs controls the verb even after a lot of." data-fix="A lot of chairs are ready."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence has correct noun-based agreement?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A lot of chairs are ready.">A lot of chairs are ready.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A lot of chairs is ready.">A lot of chairs is ready.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A lot chairs are ready.">A lot chairs are ready.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect and retrieve</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path without looking back</h3>
    <p>How can one supply be described with <span class="ex">much</span> through a noncount noun and <span class="ex">many</span> through a unit noun? Why is “questions and negatives use much or many; positives use a lot of” only a tendency? What changes between <span class="ex">a few / few</span> and <span class="ex">a little / little</span>?</p>
  </div>
  <p class="note-line">Return tomorrow before rereading. Complete the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute next-day retrieval</a>, then revisit only the noun package, unit, polarity, register, quantity scale, agreement, or spoken pattern that still feels slow.</p>

